   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the correction law, in relation to requiring that websites\nproviding incarcerated individual information be searchable by the\nincarcerated individual's name, former name or alias",
    "basePrintNo": "S4061",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4061-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 1,
       "fullName": "Anthony H. Palumbo",
       "imgName": "666_anthony_h._palumbo.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1489,
       "sessionMemberId": 2041,
       "sessionYear": 2023,
       "shortName": "PALUMBO"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §9, Cor L",
    "lawSection": "Correction Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4061\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the correction law, in relation to requiring that\nwebsites providing incarcerated individual information be searchable by\nthe incarcerated individual's name, former name or alias\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to allow the public to be able to search the\nDepartment of Corrections inmate information database by the inmate's\ncurrent legal name, their former legal name, or any known alias.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill would amend Section 9 of the Correction Law to\nprovide that any website that allows the public to search for inmate\ninformation will be programmed in such a way to allow for the public to\nsearch by the inmate's current name, any former legal name, or any other\nknown alias of the inmate.\n\nSection 2 of this bill provides that the effective date shall take\neffect on the ninetieth day after it shall have become a law.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nWhen an inmate legally changes his or her name, the general public, and\nmore specifically victims of the inmate's crime, may not be made aware\nof this name change. As a result, the public, and more importantly the\nvictim, will no longer be able to search for the inmate by the inmate's\nformer name. This causes significant problems for victims trying to\naccess information on the inmate. In order to make searching easier for\nvictims, the website that allows the public to search for inmate infor-\nmation should be searchable by the inmate's current name and any former\nname. This way a victim will be able to search for the inmate by his or\nher former name or alias, if necessary.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-22: S.4812-A (Reichlin-Melnick) - Referred to Crime Victims, Crime\nand Correction.\n\n2019-20: S.3536 (Carlucci) - Referred to Crime Victims, Crime and\nCorrection.\n\n2017-18: S.785 (Carlucci) - Passed Senate.\n\n2015-16: S.1745 (Carlucci) - Referred to Crime Victims, Crime and\nCorrection Committee.\n\n2013-14: S.1209 (Carlucci) - Referred to Crime Victims, Crime and\nCorrection Committee.  To be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
